Original commit body from f453d52b9774fb66e301dc9e325d754a98b452f2:

CfgBuilder._process_switch gave the scrutinee block no "no case
matched" edge: its only successors were the arms, so in a switch with
no default a definition killed in every arm did not reach the code
after it. `t := source(); switch x { case 1: t = "c" }; sink(t)` had
reaching definitions {("t", 6, 8)} only -- the source's t vanished,
which REMOVES reaching definitions, the direction that can manufacture
a walk False (and, since WI-kabif, delete a real flow).

The scrutinee now ALWAYS has a fall-through fringe edge. Recognising a
default arm is per grammar (Go default_case, Java/C default, Python
case _), and the edge an exhaustive switch gains never runs, so it only
ADDS definitions -- the conservative side, as the item prescribed.
WI-faful's no-recognised-arm edge is subsumed.

Tests: the Go switch and Python match repros (core, defines/uses set by
hand so no language extractor is needed). Three statement-model tests
pinned the scrutinee's successor list to the arms alone; they now
include the fall-through. Measured against dev (verify-claims): beads
(Go) and feast (Python) moved no verdict, evidence count or
analysis-method count.

